# Component Patterns

## shadcn/ui Usage

- Always use shadcn/ui primitives for standard UI elements (Button, Input, Label, Dialog, Select, Table, Badge, Card, etc.)
- Import from `@/components/ui/` — never install UI libraries that duplicate shadcn functionality
- Use the `cn()` utility from `@/lib/utils` for all conditional classNames
- Extend shadcn components via composition, not modification of the `ui/` files

## Component Structure

```tsx
/** Brief description of what this component does */
"use client"; // only if needed

import { cn } from "@/lib/utils";

interface MyComponentProps { /* typed props */ }

export function MyComponent({ ...props }: MyComponentProps) {
  return ( /* JSX */ );
}
```

## Rules

- Prefer Server Components. Only add `"use client"` when the component needs interactivity.
- Never pass functions or React components across the server/client boundary.
- Keep components focused: if it renders more than one distinct section, split it.
- Co-locate types with components when they are only used by that component.
